Q1.Why use action method .
An Action Method is a public method inside a Controller that handles an HTTP request, performs the required processing, and returns a response such as a View, JSON, Redirect, or File.

Q2. RedirectToAction() ?
RedirectToAction() tells the browser:
"Go to another Action Method."
It does not return a View directly. Instead, it sends the browser to a different URL.
RedirectToAction("ActionMethodName", "ControllerName")
•	"Welcome" → Action Method name 
•	"Home" → Controller name (HomeController)
